"faq_question_1" = "How do I start a match quickly?";
"faq_answer_1" = "On Home, pick a sport, or open New match for more options. Add frequent sports and setups to Quick start so the next match opens faster.\n\nSports that need team names, sets, format, or serving rules open Game setup first. After confirming, the scoreboard opens; some settings can still be adjusted during scoring.";
"faq_question_2" = "How do I score and fix mistakes?";
"faq_answer_2" = "Ball sports usually let you tap the left/right or top/bottom side to award a point, while sets, serve, and side changes follow the rules. Basketball, football, and simple scoreboards show common point values. Billiards, archery, boxing, and card games use score, round, or result panels.\n\nIf you make a mistake, use Undo or Back first. For manual fixes, open the edit/settings entry from the scoreboard. Not every sport has separate plus and minus buttons.";
"faq_question_3" = "I left the scoreboard. How do I continue or review it?";
"faq_answer_3" = "On the Home tab, an unfinished match shows a bottom banner (Continue match); tap it to resume scoring right where you left off. Finished and saved matches are available in Records.\n\nIf the entry is gone, the match may have ended, been deleted, or local data may have been cleared. Records are mainly for reviewing results and may not support continuing the original match flow.";
"faq_question_4" = "How do I delete records or clear data?";
"faq_answer_4" = "During a match, use Undo, Back, or the edit entry if the current sport supports it.\n\nFor saved matches, open the item in Records and delete it there. Me → Clear data removes local scoring, timer, unfinished match, saved record, and some local setting data. This cannot be undone.";
"faq_question_5" = "How do I connect a display or another phone?";
"faq_answer_5" = "To show scores on another phone or tablet, on the display device open Sync score → Join match and follow the page to create a code or QR code; connect from the controller side after entering a match and the score syncs to the display. Keep both devices online and avoid locking the screen or moving the app to the background; if sync gets stuck, leave on both sides and reconnect.\n\nTo cast the scoreboard to a TV or large screen, use your phone system wireless display (Miracast). Open wireless display from the system Control Center and connect to the TV; once the app detects the connected screen, the scoreboard appears on it automatically. The app relies on the system cast and cannot search for TVs on its own, and disconnecting the system cast also ends the projection. Different brands may name it differently (e.g. wireless display or multi-screen interaction); complete the connection in the system first.";
"faq_question_6" = "I cannot find my sport. What should I do?";
"faq_answer_6" = "Start with the closest sport. If only names, sets, teams, or starting order differ, adjust them in Game setup and add the setup to Quick start.\n\nIf the current sports cannot cover the rules, send Feedback with the sport name, common format, scoring method, and expected flow.";
"faq_question_7" = "How do membership, sign-in, and new devices work?";
"faq_answer_7" = "Membership benefits and purchase records are tied to the current account. Sign in before buying, redeeming, or restoring membership. On a new device, sign in with the same account and refresh Membership Center.\n\nIf payment succeeds but membership is not active, refresh the membership page first. If it is still wrong, send Feedback with the order number, purchase time, and signed-in account.";
"faq_question_8" = "How do I report a problem or suggest a feature?";
"faq_answer_8" = "Open Me → Feedback and choose bug report or feature suggestion. Include the sport, steps, expected result, and actual result. For display or membership issues, also include device model, system version, and app version.";
"faq_question_10" = "How do I back up my data or move it to a new phone?";
"faq_answer_10" = "Sign in to your account so your common names, places, and match records are tied to it. With the membership Cloud sync, your data syncs across devices. On a new phone, sign in with the same account and your data restores automatically. Without sign-in, data is stored only on the current device.";
"faq_question_11" = "How are my data and privacy handled?";
"faq_answer_11" = "The Privacy Policy explains what data is used and why. The microphone is used only when recording voice notes, and the camera only when scanning a QR code to sign in; both are processed locally on your device.";
